pyEzvizApi
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

lib/protocol.js and lib/control.js are a JavaScript port of parts of
pyezvizapi 2.5.1 by Renier Moorcroft, https://github.com/RenierM26/pyEzvizApi,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. pyezvizapi 2.5.1 ships no NOTICE
file.

The port is a modified, partial work. It was rewritten in JavaScript and kept
to one code path (log in, then send one control frame).

Ported, from pyezvizapi/streaming/local/hcnetsdk/:

  requests.py       hcnetsdk_command_port_execute_template,
                    read_hcnetsdk_tcp_frame (including the short-ack rule),
                    _hcnetsdk_command_port_username,
                    _hcnetsdk_command_port_md5_hmac,
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_public_key_der,
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_rsa_key
  api.py            HcNetSdkCommandPortClient.login (handshake order) and the
                    constants it uses (login family and header word, login
                    seed prefix and suffix, username length, RSA size,
                    password-seed and proof lengths, default user "admin")
  authentication.py hcnetsdk_command_port_login_request_frame,
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_password_digest,
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_login_proof,
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_login_proof_frame,
                    decode_hcnetsdk_command_port_login_challenge,
                    _hcnetsdk_command_port_login_prefix
  discovery.py      parse_hcnetsdk_command_port_login_session,
                    parse_hcnetsdk_tcp_frame_header
  protocol_types/wire_crypto.py
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_auth_word, the four-round AES-128
                    variant and its helpers, _hcnetsdk_command_port_auth_mask,
                    _hcnetsdk_command_port_local_ip_word
  protocol_types/framing.py
                    build_hcnetsdk_tcp_frame,
                    hcnetsdk_command_port_control_frame,
                    HcNetSdkCommandPortControlTemplate.to_frame

Changes from the original:

  - RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 decryption is done with BigInt instead of PyCryptodome
    (the block must start 00 02, have at least eight non-zero padding bytes,
    then 00).
  - The AES S-box is computed at load time instead of tabled.
  - Each connect, write and frame read has its own timeout, and a declared
    frame longer than 64 KiB is rejected.
  - Not ported: the login-candidate fallbacks, port 8443/TLS login, the
    control-template addend, addend_delta, mask_seed and body-tail
    transforms, media streaming, STDXML/ISAPI and config reads.

The test fixtures in test/fixtures/ were recorded by running pyezvizapi 2.5.1
against a fake camera on 127.0.0.1 with a fake password, a fake serial number
and a throwaway RSA key.

Not from pyezvizapi: the PTZ command id and body layout (ptzFrameTail and PTZ
in lib/control.js), lib/move.js, lib/probe.js, lib/rtsp.js and lib/cli.js.
The PTZ values come from our own observation of a camera we own; see
docs/PROTOCOL.md. Nothing in this package comes from vendor SDK binaries,
headers or decompiled code.

